orac-branding (1.3.3-1) umbra; urgency=medium

  * One status indicator per splash. Plymouth keeps the slim progress bar (it
    tracks real boot progress) and drops the pulsing dots; the bar hides
    under the drive-unlock prompt. The KDE login splash drops its dots and
    spinner for the same slim gradient bar, filled by the KSplash stage.
  * KDE login splash: the ORAC core video from the web dashboard plays once,
    muted, over the still picture, which stays as the fallback. Needs
    qml6-module-qtmultimedia, already in Recommends.
  * Both splashes show the web dashboard's wordmark: lowercase "orac" in
    Inter Bold, tight tracking, orange-pink-purple gradient. Plymouth cannot
    draw gradient text, so tools/build_wordmark.py pre-renders wordmark.png.
  * Terminal banner: the ORAC letters take the Orac gradient, one colour per
    letter (orange, coral, pink, purple), with "ORAC WORKSTATION" and "on
    SHADOWFETCH LINUX // NEURAL CORE ONLINE" beneath; keys are orange.

 -- Rick Masterson <rickm1982@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000

orac-branding (1.3.2-1) umbra; urgency=medium

  * Boot splash: the GRUB background (the ORAC core over black) now fills the
    screen behind the splash, scaled to cover and centred, so the boot menu's
    picture carries on through Plymouth. The fixed 320 px emblem is dropped;
    it looked far too big at boot resolutions. The wordmark, dots, slim bar
    and boot message sit under the core.

